ptimize), and _PyImport_FrozenBootstrap, _PyImport_FrozenStdlib"] [94 1 "// and _PyImport_FrozenTest (Python/frozen.c's const struct _frozen *, each pointing to its table: name, code, size,"] [95 1 "// is_package, 24 bytes an entry, a zero entry last; the code is the frozen module's marshalled code object, its name"] [96 1 "// and code kept in the world). 0 for any other name, or when the data cannot be made."] [144 1 "// cbuf is a ctypes object's own memory: size bytes of the world's heap, zeroed, freed when the Go value it belongs to"] [145 1 "// is collected (the free queued on the library, run before its next call, as arbace/clib's Defer)."] [161 1 "// keepBytes is a copy of b in the world's memory with a terminating NUL (a bytes object passed as char *: CPython"] [162 1 "// hands C the object's own buffer; here its copy, kept alive by the ctypes object that holds it)."] [164 2 "// zeroed past the data for a wchar_t's width (queue 594: test_capi's PyUnicodeWriterTest.test_widechar reads b''"] [165 2 "// with a negative size, wcslen over it, as CPython's bytes' padding after ob_sval ends it)"] [173 1 "// keepWide is s as a NUL-terminated wchar_t string (UTF-32, ci's wchar_t) in the world's memory."] [184 1 "// The keep object a setter returns (the ctypes object's b_objects holds it): a buffer kept alive."] [191 1 "// The handles' reference counts (queue 262; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: 262\"): a proxy's ob_refcnt counts"] [192 1 "// the references C holds, Python's own references being Go's. A proxy is made with count 0 (a borrowed reference: an"] [193 1 "// argument, a container's item); a new reference C receives raises it (newRef), Py_DecRef lowers it. A proxy whose"] [194 1 "// count is 0 is released when the outermost C entry ends (capiLeave: a ctypes foreign call, an extension module's"] [195 1 "// function, its PyInit), after the result was taken: its map entries dropped (the object is Go's again alone) and its"] [196 1 "// memory freed. A borrowed reference is so valid until the Python code that called C runs again, as CPython's while"] [197 1 "// its owner holds it. Types and the singletons are immortal (never released): their count is CPython's"] [198 1 "// _Py_IMMORTAL_INITIAL_REFCNT, which Include/refcount.h's inline Py_INCREF leaves alone (>= it) and Py_DECREF too"] [199 1 "// (_Py_IsImmortal: >= _Py_IMMORTAL_MINIMUM_REFCNT)."] [201 24 "// _Py_IMMORTAL_INITIAL_REFCNT (64 bits)"] [202 24 "// _Py_IMMORTAL_MINIMUM_REFCNT"] [206 19 "// the proxies whose count was 0 at some point since the last release"] [207 19 "// the C entries in progress (capiEnter, capiLeave)"] [210 1 "// handle is o's PyObject *: its proxy's address (made on the first use: ob_refcnt 0, or immortal for a type; ob_type"] [211 1 "// its type's handle)."] [221 21 "// a C-born object (queue 268): its memory"] [224 27 "// a C type's instance over a built-in base (queue 269): its memory"] [227 2 "// the head of a PyVarObject (Include/object.h): ob_refcnt, ob_type and ob_size, which the limited API's inline"] [228 2 "// Py_SIZE reads (queue 262: PySlice_GetIndicesEx's macro over a list); since queue 269 a type's PyTypeObject and"] [229 2 "// a tuple's, list's, bytes' or float's mirror (capi_mirror.go)"] [236 33 "// a C metaclass's instance (queue 270b): its C tail after the PyHeapTypeObject"] [243 24 "// queue 521: PyModuleObject, md_state read in place"] [247 27 "// queue 568: PyCMethodObject, PyCFunction_GET_SELF and GET_FUNCTION read in place"] [251 13 "// PyStructObject: s_size, s_len, s_codes, s_format, weakreflist (queue 473: _testbuffer's get_nmemb)"] [277 29 "// a type, or a small int (CPython's are immortal: -5 to 256, queue 269)"] [282 35 "// ob_type: its type's handle"] [294 1 "// fromHandle is the object a PyObject * names (nil for NULL or an address that is no proxy)."] [302 23 "// queue 521: a static object of a C type (datetime's utc_timezone)"] [310 1 "// incRef and decRef are Py_IncRef and Py_DecRef on a handle (NULL and the immortal left alone)."] [336 1 "// steal takes C's reference to o's proxy for Python (a new reference C returned: Go holds the object from now on)."] [339 1 "// pin is a reference C's memory keeps for the process (a py_object stored into a ctypes object's memory, or returned"] [340 1 "// by a callback: CPython's object is kept by the ctypes object's _objects, which pyi's handles cannot follow)."] [347 1 "// unpinWith gives the pin of the handle h back once holder is collected (on the library's next call, as cbuf's free)."] [353 1 "// capiEnter and capiLeave bracket a C entry from Python: capiLeave of the outermost releases the proxies C no longer"] [354 1 "// holds and the strings PyArg_ParseTuple handed C. Usage: defer capiLeave(capiEnter())."] [358 3 "// the C-born objects Go collected: their tp_dealloc (queue 268), inside the entry (queue 473: a dealloc that"] [359 3 "// enters C again, ndarray_dealloc's PyBuffer_Release of a view, must not leave the outermost entry and release"] [360 3 "// the handles this entry's caller just made for it)"] [375 19 "// queue 594: tstate->context taken back when C returns (cleared by C: the thread's cleared)"] [379 21 "// Py_AddPendingCall's, when C has returned to Python (py-capi-1122)"] [383 1 "// releaseUnowned releases every proxy of count 0 (outside any C entry)."] [391 2 "// a free runs the library's deferred work first (unpinWith's), which may add to the list: taken before; a"] [392 2 "// mirror released gives its items back, which may release them too (queue 269): until none is left"] [404 14 "// a C-born object's memory is its own: freed by its tp_dealloc once Go collects it (queue 268)"] [407 14 "// so is a C type's instance over a built-in base (queue 269)"] [419 1 "// varProxies are the proxies of the mutable variable-size objects (lists, bytearrays), whose ob_size refreshSizes"] [420 1 "// keeps current."] [423 1 "// varSize is ob_size of the variable-size objects CPython gives one (tuples, lists, bytes, bytearrays) and whether it"] [424 1 "// can change."] [427 37 "// tuples, lists and bytes are mirrors since queue 269"] [431 32 "// ma_used, at ob_size's offset (PyDict_GET_SIZE, queue 270)"] [439 1 "// refreshSizes writes the current ob_size of the mutable proxies (after a native: C reads it inline, and the native"] [440 1 "// may have run Python code that resized the object)."] [453 1 "// liveHandles is the number of proxies (the probe's count of the handles C keeps)."] [456 1 "// isSmallInt is an exact int of -5 to 256 (pyi's are interned as CPython's, which are immortal)."] [466 1 "// goMap is a Python buffer's bytes mapped into the world's address space (queue 261: from_buffer shares a bytearray's,"] [467 1 "// an array's or a memoryview's memory, as CPython's ctypes object points into the exporter's buffer): a slab at a free"] [468 1 "// address of the mappings' region whose bytes are the buffer's own, so C, the ctypes object and Python see each"] [469 1 "// other's writes. The exporter cannot move them while the ctypes object keeps its memoryview (a resize is refused)."] [472 1 "// mapGo maps b; the mapping is removed once the goMap is collected (on the library's next call, as cbuf's free)."] [486 1 "// bufferAddress is array.buffer_info()'s address once _ctypes is imported (queue 598; py.ExtBufferAddress): b mapped into"] [487 1 "// the world as from_buffer maps it, so from_address of the address reads and writes the array's items in place, as"] [488 1 "// CPython's ctypes object at the array's ob_item. The mapping is kept by the array and made again when its buffer moved"] [489 1 "// (a resize, as CPython's ob_item moves)."] [498 1 "// goBufMap is an array's buffer and its mapping (bufferAddress)."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[51 36] [53 49] [68 28] [71 30] [75 27] [82 32] [98 22] [216 25] [220 19] [223 19] [235 30] [269 34] [296 21] [304 23] [316 21] [403 25] [409 23] [428 25] [432 24] [447 28] [491 30]]} (go/file "world.go" :imports [

